Taffey Lewis?

418
00:49:33,387 --> 00:49:35,264
- Taffey.
- Yeah?

419
00:49:35,890 --> 00:49:38,142
I'd like to ask you a few questions.

420
00:49:38,309 --> 00:49:40,102
Blow.

421
00:49:41,770 --> 00:49:44,064
You ever buy snakes
from the Egyptian, Taffey?

422
00:49:44,231 --> 00:49:45,733
All the time, pal.

423
00:49:48,569 --> 00:49:49,904
You ever see this girl, huh?

424
00:49:51,405 --> 00:49:52,865
Never seen her. Buzz off.

425
00:49:53,032 --> 00:49:54,909
Your licenses in order, pal?

426
00:49:55,659 --> 00:49:57,161
Hey, Louie.

427
00:49:57,328 --> 00:50:01,916
The man is dry. Give him one
on the house, okay? See?

428
00:50:44,291 --> 00:50:45,960
<i>Hello?</i>

429
00:50:47,836 --> 00:50:51,465
I've had people walk out on me before,
but not when...

430
00:50:51,632 --> 00:50:53,801
...I was being so charming.

431
00:50:54,009 --> 00:50:58,097
I'm in a bar, here now,
down in the Fourth Sector.

432
00:50:59,181 --> 00:51:00,641
Taffey Lewis is on the line.

433
00:51:00,808 --> 00:51:03,978
Why don't you come on down here
and have a drink?

434
00:51:04,144 --> 00:51:06,689
<i>I don't think so, Mr. Deckard.</i>

435
00:51:07,898 --> 00:51:09,233
<i>That's not my kind of place.</i>

436
00:51:09,900 --> 00:51:10,985
Go someplace else?

437
00:51:26,875 --> 00:51:29,420
MAN <i>Ladies and gentlemen...</i>

438
00:51:29,628 --> 00:51:34,842
<i>...Taffey Lewis presents
Miss Salome and the snake.</i>

439
00:51:35,009 --> 00:51:39,388
<i>Watch her take the pleasure
from the serpent...</i>

440
00:51:39,555 --> 00:51:43,350
<i>...that once corrupted man.</i>

441
00:52:25,559 --> 00:52:28,270
Excuse me, Miss Salome,
can I talk to you for a minute?

442
00:52:28,437 --> 00:52:32,566
I'm from the American Federation
of Variety Artists.

443
00:52:32,733 --> 00:52:33,776
Oh, yeah?

444
00:52:33,942 --> 00:52:37,738
I'm not here to make you join.
No, ma'am. That's not my department.

445
00:52:37,905 --> 00:52:39,782
Actually...

446
00:52:41,950 --> 00:52:46,413
...I'm from the Confidential Committee
on Moral Abuses.

447
00:52:47,331 --> 00:52:49,166
Committee of Moral Abuses?

448
00:52:49,333 --> 00:52:51,502
There's been reports
that the management...

449
00:52:51,710 --> 00:52:53,837
...has been taking liberties
with the artists.

450
00:52:54,004 --> 00:52:55,464
I don't know nothing about it.

451
00:52:55,631 --> 00:52:58,634
Have you felt yourself to be
exploited in any way?

452
00:52:58,801 --> 00:53:01,261
How do you mean "exploited"?

453
00:53:01,428 --> 00:53:03,972
Well, like to get this job.

454
00:53:04,139 --> 00:53:09,103
I mean, did you do, or were you
asked to do, anything that's...

455
00:53:09,269 --> 00:53:11,438
...lewd or unsavory or...

456
00:53:11,605 --> 00:53:15,484
...otherwise repulsive
to your person, huh?

457
00:53:18,529 --> 00:53:21,115
- Are you for real?
- Oh, yeah.

458
00:53:21,281 --> 00:53:24,493
I'd like to check
your dressing room, if I may.

459
00:53:24,660 --> 00:53:27,371
- For what?
- For holes.

460
00:53:27,538 --> 00:53:28,622
Holes?

461
00:53:28,789 --> 00:53:31,542
Well, you'd be surprised
what a guy would go through...

462
00:53:31,750 --> 00:53:34,545
...to get a glimpse of a beautiful body.

463
00:53:37,756 --> 00:53:38,841
No, I wouldn't.

464
00:53:39,007 --> 00:53:41,135
Little...

465
00:53:41,301 --> 00:53:46,807
...dirty holes they drill in the wall
so they can watch a lady undress.

466
00:54:20,174 --> 00:54:23,469
- Is this a real snake?
- Of course it's not real.

467
00:54:23,635 --> 00:54:27,806
Think I'd be working in a place like this
if I could afford a real snake?

468
00:54:41,862 --> 00:54:44,865
So if somebody does try to exploit me,
who do I go to about it?

469
00:54:45,032 --> 00:54:49,203
- Me.
- You're a dedicated man. Dry me.

470
00:55:15,604 --> 00:55:17,397
The only thing they care about--

471
00:55:17,564 --> 00:55:18,774
Hey!

472
00:56:45,485 --> 00:56:48,196
<i>Cross now. Cross now.</i>

473
00:56:48,363 --> 00:56:51,533
<i>Cross now. Cross now.</i>

474
00:56:51,700 --> 00:56:54,411
<i>Cross now. Cross now.</i>

475
00:56:54,578 --> 00:56:57,497
<i>Cross now. Cross now.</i>

476
00:56:57,664 --> 00:57:01,001
<i>Cross now. Cross now.</i>

477
00:57:01,668 --> 00:57:03,837
<i>Don't walk. Don't walk.</i>

478
00:57:04,004 --> 00:57:06,089
<i>Don't walk. Don't walk.</i>

479
00:57:06,256 --> 00:57:09,343
<i>Don't walk. Don't walk. Don't walk.</i>

480
00:57:24,024 --> 00:57:27,152
<i>Cross now. Cross now.</i>

481
00:57:27,486 --> 00:57:30,238
<i>Cross now. Cross now.</i>

482
00:57:30,405 --> 00:57:32,699
<i>Cross now. Cross now.</i>

483
00:57:33,367 --> 00:57:36,370
<i>Cross now. Cross now.</i>

484
00:57:36,536 --> 00:57:38,121
<i>Cross now. Cross now.</i>

485
00:57:38,288 --> 00:57:40,123
Move! Get out of the way!

486
00:59:26,480 --> 00:59:28,023
Deckard.

487
00:59:28,190 --> 00:59:29,816
B26354.

488
00:59:36,323 --> 00:59:38,992
<i>Move on. Move on.</i>

489
00:59:39,159 --> 00:59:41,453
<i>Move on. Move on.</i>

490
00:59:41,620 --> 00:59:44,873
<i>Move on. Move on.</i>

491
00:59:50,504 --> 00:59:52,214
A minute.

492
00:59:54,508 --> 00:59:56,009
Yeah, what do you want?

493
00:59:56,176 --> 00:59:58,011
Tsingtao.

494
01:00:05,185 --> 01:00:07,062
This enough?

495
01:00:07,229 --> 01:00:08,730
Yeah.

496
01:00:17,405 --> 01:00:19,241
Bryant.

497
01:00:39,177 --> 01:00:43,098
Christ, Deckard, you look almost as bad
as that skin-job you left on the sidewalk.

498
01:00:43,265 --> 01:00:44,558
I'm going home.

499
01:00:44,724 --> 01:00:46,601
Could learn from this guy, Gaff.

500
01:00:46,768 --> 01:00:49,563
He's a goddamn one-man
slaughterhouse, that's what he is.

501
01:00:50,397 --> 01:00:52,107
Four more to go.

502
01:00:52,274 --> 01:00:54,067
- Come on, Gaff, let's go.
- Three.

503
01:00:56,319 --> 01:00:57,487
There's three to go.

504
01:00:58,113 --> 01:01:00,407
There's four.

505
01:01:00,574 --> 01:01:03,368
That skin-job you VK'd
at the Tyrell Corporation...

506
01:01:03,535 --> 01:01:07,414
...Rachael, disappeared, vanished.
Didn't even know she was a Replicant.

507
01:01:07,581 --> 01:01:10,417
Something to do with a brain implant,
says Tyrell.

508
01:01:10,584 --> 01:01:13,962
Come on, Gaff.
Drink some for me, huh, pal?

509
01:01:58,632 --> 01:01:59,633
Leon.

510
01:01:59,799 --> 01:02:01,509
How old am I?

511
01:02:05,639 --> 01:02:07,515
I don't know.

512
01:02:09,809 --> 01:02:13,021
My birthday's April 10, 2017.
How long do I live?

513
01:02:13,188 --> 01:02:14,981
Four years.

514
01:02:21,988 --> 01:02:23,281
More than you.

515
01:02:28,286 --> 01:02:30,997
Painful to live in fear, isn't it?

516
01:02:36,544 --> 01:02:39,839
Nothing is worse than having
an itch you can never scratch.

517
01:02:40,799 --> 01:02:42,175
I agree.

518
01:02:53,353 --> 01:02:55,313
Wake up. Time to die.

519
01:03:30,390 --> 01:03:32,267
Shakes?

520
01:03:33,893 --> 01:03:35,437
Me too.

521
01:03:39,399 --> 01:03:41,359
I get them bad.

522
01:03:46,906 --> 01:03:49,075
It's part of the business.

523
01:03:56,374 --> 01:03:57,751
I'm not in the business.

524
01:04:11,264 --> 01:04:13,475
I am the business.

525
01:05:46,401 --> 01:05:47,694
What if I go north?

526
01:05:51,906 --> 01:05:53,867
Disappear.

527
01:05:58,204 --> 01:05:59,539
Would you come after me?

528
01:06:01,708 --> 01:06:03,376
Hunt me?

529
01:06:08,131 --> 01:06:09,757
No.

530
01:06:12,427 --> 01:06:14,429
No, I wouldn't.

531
01:06:20,226 --> 01:06:21,394
I owe you one.

532
01:06:36,618 --> 01:06:38,912
But somebody would.

533
01:06:51,257 --> 01:06:53,134
Deckard...

534
01:06:55,595 --> 01:06:57,764
...you know those files on me?

535
01:06:59,098 --> 01:07:02,769
The incept date. The longevity.

536
01:07:02,936 --> 01:07:04,812
Those things.

537
01:07:06,147 --> 01:07:07,982
You saw them?

538
01:07:11,444 --> 01:07:13,154
They're...

539
01:07:13,321 --> 01:07:14,531
...classified.

540
01:07:14,697 --> 01:07:17,200
But you're a policeman.

541
01:07:17,367 --> 01:07:19,452
I...

542
01:07:19,619 --> 01:07:21,621
...didn't look at them.

543
01:07:23,665 --> 01:07:25,959
You know,
that Voight-Kampff test of yours...

544
01:07:27,001 --> 01:07:29,963
...did you ever take that test yourself?

545
01:07:41,683 --> 01:07:43,309
Deckard.

546
01:10:13,793 --> 01:10:15,503
I dreamt music.

547
01:10:20,675 --> 01:10:23,302
I didn't know if I could play.

548
01:10:24,971 --> 01:10:27,765
I remember lessons.

549
01:10:28,641 --> 01:10:32,562
I don't know if it's me
or Tyrell's niece.

550
01:10:37,150 --> 01:10:39,485
You play beautifully.

551
01:11:49,555 --> 01:11:52,058
Now you kiss me.

552
01:11:53,434 --> 01:11:54,894
I can't rely on my--

553
01:11:55,061 --> 01:11:57,730
Say, "Kiss me."

554
01:12:00,441 --> 01:12:02,360
Kiss me.

555
01:12:13,788 --> 01:12:15,748
I want you.

556
01:12:18,793 --> 01:12:20,336
I want you.

557
01:12:20,503 --> 01:12:22,088
Again.

558
01:12:22,255 --> 01:12:24,131
I want you.

559
01:12:27,301 --> 01:12:29,762
Put your hands on me.

560
01:13:51,510 --> 01:13:54,805
- What you doing?
- I'm sorry. Just peeking.

561
01:13:54,972 --> 01:13:56,474
Oh.

562
01:13:58,726 --> 01:14:01,854
- How do I look?
- You look better.

563
01:14:02,021 --> 01:14:05,066
- Just better?
- Well...

564
01:14:05,232 --> 01:14:06,525
...you look beautiful.

565
01:14:10,112 --> 01:14:11,781
Thanks.

566
01:14:18,204 --> 01:14:20,122
How old are you?

567
01:14:22,041 --> 01:14:24,085
Twenty-five.

568
01:14:24,251 --> 01:14:27,213
- What's your problem?
- Methuselah syndrome.

569
01:14:27,380 --> 01:14:28,714
What's that?

570
01:14:28,881 --> 01:14:31,884
My glands, they grow old too fast.

571
01:14:33,052 --> 01:14:37,264
- Is that <i>why</i> you're still on Earth?
- Yeah. I couldn't pass the medical.

572
01:14:40,267 --> 01:14:41,477
Anyway...

573
01:14:41,644 --> 01:14:43,104
...I kind of like it here.

574
01:14:45,773 --> 01:14:47,733
I like you...

575
01:14:47,900 --> 01:14:49,151
...just the <i>way</i> you are.

576
01:14:52,405 --> 01:14:54,198
Hi, Roy.

577
01:14:54,365 --> 01:14:55,783
Hi.

578
01:14:55,950 --> 01:14:57,660
Gosh, you...

579
01:14:57,827 --> 01:15:00,121
...really got some nice toys here.

580
01:15:00,287 --> 01:15:02,665
This is the friend I was telling you about.

581
01:15:02,832 --> 01:15:06,085
This is my savior, J.F. Sebastian.

582
01:15:06,252 --> 01:15:07,753
Sebastian.

583
01:15:08,421 --> 01:15:11,090
I like a man that stays put.

584
01:15:12,633 --> 01:15:15,970
You live here all by yourself, do you?

585
01:15:16,137 --> 01:15:17,179
Yes.

586
01:15:28,774 --> 01:15:31,110
How about some breakfast?

587
01:15:31,277 --> 01:15:33,279
I was just gonna make some.

588
01:15:33,446 --> 01:15:34,447
Excuse me.

589
01:15:41,829 --> 01:15:43,456
Well?

590
01:15:45,708 --> 01:15:46,959
Leon...

591
01:15:47,126 --> 01:15:49,128
What's going on?

592
01:15:53,466 --> 01:15:55,134
There's only two of us now.

593
01:15:57,344 --> 01:16:00,473
Then we're stupid and we'll die.

594
01:16:04,477 --> 01:16:06,687
No, we won't.

595
01:16:40,179 --> 01:16:41,180
No.

596
01:16:41,347 --> 01:16:43,891
Knight takes queen, see?

597
01:16:44,058 --> 01:16:46,018
Won't do.

598
01:16:54,360 --> 01:16:56,445
Why are you staring at us, Sebastian?

599
01:16:56,654 --> 01:16:58,030
Because...

600
01:16:58,197 --> 01:17:00,366
...you're so different.

601
01:17:01,867 --> 01:17:03,953
You're so perfect.

602
01:17:06,455 --> 01:17:08,707
Yes.

603
01:17:08,874 --> 01:17:11,043
What generation are you?

604
01:17:19,176 --> 01:17:20,386
Nexus 6.

605
01:17:20,845 --> 01:17:22,763
Ah. I knew it.

606
01:17:22,930 --> 01:17:26,225
Because I do genetic design work
for the Tyrell Corporation.

607
01:17:26,392 --> 01:17:28,561
There's some of me in you.

608
01:17:29,687 --> 01:17:31,397
Show me something.

609
01:17:31,564 --> 01:17:33,315
Like what?

610
01:17:33,482 --> 01:17:35,401
Like anything.

611
01:17:37,236 --> 01:17:42,074
We're no computers, Sebastian.
We're physical.

612
01:17:43,826 --> 01:17:46,078
I think, Sebastian...

613
01:17:46,245 --> 01:17:48,664
...therefore, I am.

614
01:17:48,831 --> 01:17:52,126
Very good, Pris. Now show him why.

615
01:18:19,028 --> 01:18:20,779
We've got a lot in common.

616
01:18:20,946 --> 01:18:23,199
- What do you mean?
- Similar problems.

617
01:18:23,365 --> 01:18:26,160
Accelerated decrepitude.

618
01:18:28,037 --> 01:18:30,831
I don't know much
about biomechanics, Roy. I wish I did.

619
01:18:32,958 --> 01:18:35,461
If we don't find help soon...

620
01:18:35,628 --> 01:18:38,505
...Pris hasn't got long to live.

621
01:18:38,672 --> 01:18:40,466
We can't allow that.

622
01:18:42,635 --> 01:18:45,846
- Is he good?
- Who?

623
01:18:46,013 --> 01:18:49,391
- Your opponent.
- Oh, Dr. Tyrell?

624
01:18:49,558 --> 01:18:53,020
I've only beaten him once in chess.
He's a genius.

625
01:18:55,314 --> 01:18:56,315
He designed you.

626
01:18:58,776 --> 01:19:01,320
Maybe he could help.

627
01:19:01,487 --> 01:19:04,031
I'd be happy to mention it to him.

628
01:19:06,158 --> 01:19:09,662
Better if I talk to him in person.

629
01:19:12,748 --> 01:19:17,836
But I understand
he's a sort of hard man to get to.

630
01:19:18,003 --> 01:19:19,922
Yes.

631
01:19:20,089 --> 01:19:21,715
Very.

632
01:19:24,677 --> 01:19:27,054
Will you help us?

633
01:19:27,805 --> 01:19:29,098
I can't.

634
01:19:29,306 --> 01:19:31,267
We need you, Sebastian.

635
01:19:31,433 --> 01:19:34,353
You're our best and only friend.

636
01:19:47,366 --> 01:19:49,827
We're so happy you found us.

637
01:19:51,620 --> 01:19:53,706
I don't think
there's another human being...

638
01:19:53,872 --> 01:19:56,208
...in the whole world
who would've helped us.

639
01:20:45,132 --> 01:20:49,636
66,000 Prosser & Ankovich. Hm.

640
01:20:49,928 --> 01:20:51,347
Trade.

641
01:20:51,513 --> 01:20:54,266
- Trade at two--
<i>- Blue entry.</i>

642
01:20:55,267 --> 01:20:58,645
<i>A Mr. J.F. Sebastian.</i>

643
01:20:58,812 --> 01:21:02,941
<i>16417.</i>

644
01:21:03,692 --> 01:21:05,444
TYRELL <i>At this hour?</i>

645
01:21:05,611 --> 01:21:08,781
<i>What can I do for you, Sebastian?</i>

646
01:21:11,950 --> 01:21:13,452
Queen to bishop six. Check.

647
01:21:19,041 --> 01:21:21,210
Nonsense.

648
01:21:21,418 --> 01:21:23,629
Just a moment.

649
01:21:26,548 --> 01:21:31,303
Queen to bishop six, ridiculous.

650
01:21:36,934 --> 01:21:38,644
Queen...

651
01:21:40,312 --> 01:21:42,314
...bishop six.

652
01:21:43,315 --> 01:21:44,316
Hm.

653
01:21:47,444 --> 01:21:49,822
<i>Knight...</i>

654
01:21:49,988 --> 01:21:52,199
<i>...takes queen.</i>

655
01:21:58,997 --> 01:22:01,417
What's on your mind, Sebastian?

656
01:22:01,583 --> 01:22:03,043
What are you thinking about?

657
01:22:04,670 --> 01:22:06,880
Bishop to king seven.

658
01:22:07,047 --> 01:22:09,091
Checkmate.

659
01:22:09,258 --> 01:22:11,343
Bishop to king seven.
Checkmate, I think.

660
01:22:13,178 --> 01:22:16,390
Got a brainstorm, huh, Sebastian?

661
01:22:16,557 --> 01:22:19,518
Milk and cookies
kept you awake, huh?

662
01:22:19,685 --> 01:22:21,854
<i>Let's discuss this.</i>

663
01:22:22,020 --> 01:22:24,022
<i>You better come up, Sebastian.</i>

664
01:22:41,623 --> 01:22:43,584
Mr. Tyrell?

665
01:22:45,377 --> 01:22:47,045
I...

666
01:22:47,212 --> 01:22:49,131
I brought a friend.

667
01:22:55,387 --> 01:22:59,391
I'm surprised
you didn't come here sooner.

668
01:23:06,064 --> 01:23:09,234
It's not an easy thing
to meet your maker.

669
01:23:09,943 --> 01:23:12,905
And what can he do for you?

670
01:23:13,614 --> 01:23:17,117
Can the maker repair what he makes?

671
01:23:17,284 --> 01:23:20,621
Would you like to be modified?

672
01:23:20,787 --> 01:23:22,748
Stay here.

673
01:23:27,920 --> 01:23:31,298
Had in mind something
a little more radical.

674
01:23:31,924 --> 01:23:33,926
What...?

675
01:23:34,092 --> 01:23:36,595
What seems to be the problem?

676
01:23:36,929 --> 01:23:39,556
- Death.
- Death.

677
01:23:40,182 --> 01:23:43,268
Well, I'm afraid that's
a little out of my jurisdiction. You--

678
01:23:43,435 --> 01:23:46,438
I want more life...

679
01:23:46,605 --> 01:23:47,856
...father.

680
01:23:52,778 --> 01:23:54,947
The facts of life.

681
01:23:56,323 --> 01:23:59,117
To make an alteration in the...

682
01:23:59,284 --> 01:24:01,703
...evolvement of
an organic life system is fatal.

683
01:24:01,870 --> 01:24:05,457
A coding sequence cannot be revised
once it's been established.

684
01:24:05,624 --> 01:24:06,625
Why not?

685
01:24:06,792 --> 01:24:08,835
Because by the second day
of incubation...

686
01:24:09,002 --> 01:24:13,507
...any cells that have undergone
reversion mutations...

687
01:24:13,674 --> 01:24:17,970
...give rise to revertant colonies
like rats leaving a sinking ship.

688
01:24:18,136 --> 01:24:19,888
Then the ship sinks.

689
01:24:20,097 --> 01:24:23,642
What about EMS recombination?

690
01:24:23,809 --> 01:24:25,310
We've already tried it.

691
01:24:25,477 --> 01:24:29,815
Ethyl methane sulfonate is an
alkylating agent and a potent mutagen.

692
01:24:29,982 --> 01:24:34,069
It created a virus so lethal...

693
01:24:34,236 --> 01:24:36,405
...the subject was dead
before he left the table.

694
01:24:36,613 --> 01:24:39,658
Then a repressor protein
that blocks the operating cells.

695
01:24:39,825 --> 01:24:43,829
Wouldn't obstruct replication, but it
does give rise to an error in replication.

696
01:24:43,996 --> 01:24:48,667
So that the newly formed DNA strand
carries a mutation...

697
01:24:48,834 --> 01:24:51,712
...and you've got a virus again.

698
01:24:51,878 --> 01:24:56,341
But this, all of this, is...

699
01:24:56,508 --> 01:24:58,093
...academic.

700
01:24:58,260 --> 01:25:00,762
You were made
as well as we could make you.

701
01:25:00,929 --> 01:25:02,681
But not to last.

702
01:25:03,515 --> 01:25:06,685
The light that burns twice as bright
burns half as long.

703
01:25:06,852 --> 01:25:11,064
And you have burned
so very, very brightly, Roy.

704
01:25:11,690 --> 01:25:13,442
Look at you.

705
01:25:13,650 --> 01:25:16,194
You're the prodigal son.

706
01:25:16,361 --> 01:25:19,865
You're quite a prize.

707
01:25:25,537 --> 01:25:27,039
I've done...

708
01:25:27,205 --> 01:25:28,874
...questionable things.

709
01:25:29,041 --> 01:25:30,917
Also extraordinary things.

710
01:25:31,543 --> 01:25:33,920
Revel in your time.

711
01:25:37,883 --> 01:25:42,387
Nothing the god of biomechanics
wouldn't let you in heaven for.

712
01:26:34,606 --> 01:26:37,359
Sorry, Sebastian.

713
01:26:37,734 --> 01:26:40,737
Come. Come.

714
01:27:27,159 --> 01:27:29,494
<i>Body identified with Tyrell...</i>

715
01:27:29,661 --> 01:27:31,997
<i>...is a 25-year-old male Caucasian.</i>

716
01:27:32,164 --> 01:27:35,000
<i>Name: Sebastian, J.F. Sebastian.</i>

717
01:27:35,167 --> 01:27:40,005
<i>Address: Bradbury Apartments,
Ninth Sector, NF46751.</i>

718
01:27:40,172 --> 01:27:41,840
<i>I want you to go down there and--</i>

719
01:27:45,844 --> 01:27:48,889
<i>This sector's closed to
ground traffic. What are you doing here?</i>

720
01:27:49,055 --> 01:27:52,726
- I'm working. What are you doing?
<i>- Arresting you, that's what I'm doing.</i>

721
01:27:52,893 --> 01:27:57,606
I'm Deckard, Blade Runner.
26354. I'm filed and monitored.

722
01:27:57,814 --> 01:27:59,024
<i>Hold on. Checking.</i>

723
01:28:03,195 --> 01:28:06,907
<i>Okay. Checked and cleared.
Have a better one.</i>

724
01:28:17,459 --> 01:28:19,461
<i>- Hello.</i>
- Hi. Is J.F. there?

725
01:28:19,628 --> 01:28:23,048
<i>- Who is it?</i>
- This is Eddie, old friend of J.F.'s.

726
01:28:26,927 --> 01:28:28,637
That's no <i>way</i> to treat a friend.

727
01:31:27,232 --> 01:31:29,317
Home again, home again, jiggidy-jig.

728
01:31:30,443 --> 01:31:33,405
Good evening, J.F.

729
01:31:43,581 --> 01:31:45,417
<i>Tea?</i>

730
01:31:46,751 --> 01:31:48,586
<i>More tea?</i>

731
01:31:49,629 --> 01:31:50,672
<i>Tea?</i>

732
01:32:00,223 --> 01:32:02,100
<i>More tea?</i>

733
01:32:04,352 --> 01:32:06,104
<i>Tea?</i>

734
01:32:07,689 --> 01:32:09,607
<i>More tea?</i>

735
01:32:11,192 --> 01:32:13,153
<i>More tea?</i>

736
01:32:25,582 --> 01:32:27,459
<i>More tea?</i>

737
01:35:33,061 --> 01:35:36,814
Not very sporting to fire
on an unarmed opponent.

738
01:35:38,399 --> 01:35:41,778
I thought you were
supposed to be good.

739
01:35:43,071 --> 01:35:45,740
Aren't you the good man?

740
01:35:50,578 --> 01:35:54,249
Come on, Deckard.

741
01:35:55,416 --> 01:35:57,293
Show me...

742
01:35:58,127 --> 01:36:00,255
...what you're made of.

743
01:36:12,267 --> 01:36:14,143
Proud of yourself, little man?

744
01:36:22,068 --> 01:36:25,071
- This is for Zhora.
- Ah!

745
01:36:25,446 --> 01:36:28,116
- This is for Pris.
- Ah!

746
01:36:33,955 --> 01:36:35,456
Come on, Deckard.

747
01:36:35,999 --> 01:36:39,210
I'm right here,
but you've gotta shoot straight.

748
01:36:40,545 --> 01:36:42,964
Straight doesn't seem
to be good enough!

749
01:36:43,131 --> 01:36:44,173
Now it's my turn.

750
01:36:46,092 --> 01:36:49,804
I'm gonna give you a few seconds
before I come.

751
01:36:50,513 --> 01:36:51,806
One.

752
01:36:51,973 --> 01:36:54,183
Two.

753
01:37:06,154 --> 01:37:07,989
Three.

754
01:37:08,156 --> 01:37:10,116
Four.

755
01:37:22,378 --> 01:37:24,047
Pris.

756
01:38:09,133 --> 01:38:11,177
Ah!

757
01:38:34,617 --> 01:38:38,996
I'm coming.

758
01:38:39,205 --> 01:38:40,957
Deckard!

759
01:38:43,418 --> 01:38:44,710
<i>Four, five</i>

760
01:38:47,922 --> 01:38:51,092
<i>How to stay alive?</i>

761
01:39:13,990 --> 01:39:15,616
I can see you!

762
01:39:41,476 --> 01:39:43,728
Not yet!

763
01:39:43,895 --> 01:39:44,979
Not...

764
01:40:12,048 --> 01:40:13,090
Ah!

765
01:40:17,720 --> 01:40:19,514
Five.

766
01:40:22,725 --> 01:40:24,268
Five.

767
01:40:28,439 --> 01:40:29,607
Yes.

768
01:40:37,532 --> 01:40:39,033
You better get it up.

769
01:40:39,700 --> 01:40:41,202
Or I'm gonna have to kill you.

770
01:40:42,245 --> 01:40:44,539
Unless you're alive, you can't play.

771
01:40:44,705 --> 01:40:46,666
And if you don't play...

772
01:40:56,259 --> 01:40:58,469
<i>Six, seven</i>

773
01:40:58,678 --> 01:41:00,555
<i>Go to hell or go to heaven</i>

774
01:41:08,062 --> 01:41:09,730
Good, that's the spirit!

775
01:41:51,105 --> 01:41:53,274
That hurt.

776
01:41:56,527 --> 01:41:58,654
That was irrational of you.

777
01:42:00,615 --> 01:42:01,949
Not to mention...

778
01:42:02,617 --> 01:42:04,952
...unsportsmanlike.

779
01:42:08,998 --> 01:42:11,000
Where are you going?

780
01:45:15,476 --> 01:45:19,355
Quite an experience to live in fear,
isn't it?

781
01:45:21,065 --> 01:45:24,151
That's what it is to be a slave.

782
01:46:23,043 --> 01:46:24,295
I've...

783
01:46:24,461 --> 01:46:29,550
...seen things
you people wouldn't believe.

784
01:46:31,093 --> 01:46:36,265
Attack ships on fire
off the shoulder of Orion.

785
01:46:38,225 --> 01:46:40,561
I watched C-beams...

786
01:46:40,728 --> 01:46:44,398
...glitter in the dark
near the Tannhäuser Gate.

787
01:46:48,569 --> 01:46:50,613
All those...

788
01:46:50,779 --> 01:46:53,824
...moments will be lost...

789
01:46:53,991 --> 01:46:56,243
...in time...

790
01:46:57,786 --> 01:47:00,080
...like...

791
01:47:00,247 --> 01:47:01,957
...tears...

792
01:47:03,417 --> 01:47:05,628
...in rain.

793
01:47:09,256 --> 01:47:11,800
Time to die.

794
01:48:17,741 --> 01:48:20,661
You've done a man's job, sir.

795
01:48:26,333 --> 01:48:28,711
I guess you're through, huh?

796
01:48:30,754 --> 01:48:32,548
Finished.

797
01:48:54,570 --> 01:48:57,573
It's too bad she won't live.

798
01:48:58,574 --> 01:49:01,076
But then again, who does?

799
01:49:34,735 --> 01:49:36,570
Rachael?

800
01:49:44,286 --> 01:49:46,038
Rachael?

801
01:49:59,927 --> 01:50:01,470
Rachael?

802
01:51:08,203 --> 01:51:09,997
Do you love me?

803
01:51:11,165 --> 01:51:12,875
I love you.

804
01:51:13,750 --> 01:51:15,669
Do you trust me?

805
01:51:16,837 --> 01:51:18,839
I trust you.

806
01:51:28,348 --> 01:51:29,892
Rachael?

807
01:52:09,473 --> 01:52:12,392
<i>It's too bad she won't live.</i>

808
01:52:12,559 --> 01:52:15,187
<i>But then again, who does?</i>

